    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d155">

                <pb facs="0175" n="163" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg163"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841D.24/24: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ireland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dublin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-08-15T17:00:00+01:00">August 15, 1940—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 15—1:22 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>168 [<hi rendition="#italic">68</hi>]. Reference Department’s telegram No. 39,
                    June 20, 4 p.m.,<anchor n="6" xml:id="d155-f1"/> Irish Premier today informs me
                    that purchase of rifles appears stalemated <pb facs="0176" n="164"
                        xml:id="pg164"/> in Washington. Is there yet hope for delivery. Need for
                    these arms unquestionably pressing.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
